WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.890
The CW certainly knows its brand, and the
company is shooting right down the middle

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.700
with 2018's breakout hit, All American.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.490
The series is a dramatization of the real-life
story of Spencer Paysinger, a star football

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.760
player from South Los Angeles who beat the
odds to make it all the way to the NFL, where

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.130
he played linebacker for the New York Giants.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.110
Spencer James is the lead character of the
show, based loosely on Paysinger.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:27.890
His fish-out-of-water story has captivated
audiences from the get-go, earning All American

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.390
an early renewal for not just a second season,
but also a third.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.280
"It's the story of an outsider, of a person
who's just trying to find who they are in

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.280
this world."

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.500
If the fresh-faced young actor portraying
the charismatic safety looks familiar to you,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.960
there's probably a reason why.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.850
Spencer James is played by Daniel Ezra, an
accomplished young actor and veteran of both

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.329
the stage and TV.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:52.960
Let's break down the roles that led him here,
and highlight the projects you might have

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:53.960
seen him in before.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.069
Being an English actor, born in Birmingham
in the West Midlands, Daniel Ezra naturally

00:00:58.069 --> 00:01:00.800
kicked off his professional career in British
productions.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.750
He began acting in 2014, making his small-screen
debut in the television movie Murdered by

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.920
My Boyfriend.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.350
Ezra then landed a one-off role on the BBC
drama series The Village and the critically-acclaimed

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.460
movie Blood Cells in 2014.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.350
In 2016, Ezra scored the role of Dan Johnson
on Undercover, a six-part BBC drama that centers

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:23.450
on a human rights barrister fighting to free
an American inmate from death row.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:28.360
Fans may also recognize Ezra as Daniel Reed
from season 2 of anthology series The Missing,

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.219
or as DC Ashton from the police procedural
Prime Suspect 1973.

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:38.520
That series rolled out in 2017, but for this
young actor, 2018 was the year that changed

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.520
everything.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.200
Before he landed the leading role on All American,
Ezra had another memorable TV turn as Nathaniel

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.520
Wilson on the British series A Discovery of
Witches.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.079
That show is an adaptation of the popular
All Souls trilogy of fantasy novels by Deborah

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:53.079
Harkness.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:57.360
The story of the series centers on Diana Bishop,
a historian and witch who discovers an ancient

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.039
grimoire in Oxford's Bodleian Library.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:04.289
This revelation proves unfortunate, as it
draws Diana deeper into a world of magic and

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:07.759
evil creatures that she would prefer to leave
well enough alone.

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:12.000
Ezra's character, Nathaniel Wilson, crops
up in the very first episode as a Daemon computer

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.060
whiz with a witch for a daughter.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:18.010
Although Ezra wasn't listed as a principal
cast member, his character recurred throughout

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.170
the first season, and had a memorable impact
on the plot.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:26.310
It was likely this appearance more than anything
else that got Ezra noticed by casting directors,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.780
and paved the way for his leading role on
All American.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.530
While the football drama is undoubtedly the
27-year-old actor's biggest break to date,

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:37.860
it's fair to say his career got a major boost
from his role on A Discovery of Witches.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:42.099
Witches was renewed for two more seasons back
in 2018, but there's been no announcement

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:43.870
regarding whether Ezra will return.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.780
We assume the CW is keeping him pretty busy.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:51.870
Back in 2017, Ezra put his classical training
to use playing Sebastian in the National Theatre's

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.720
live performance of Shakespeare's Twelfth
Night.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.160
The gender-bending comedy is one of the Bard's
most famous works, and Sebastian was a solid

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.780
role for such a new talent.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:06.390
The story of Twelfth Night concerns intersecting
cases of mistaken identity; in the play, Sebastian

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.040
is the twin brother to Viola.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.250
He's lost at sea in the first scene and presumed
dead by his sister, though it's later revealed

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.739
that he survived the shipwreck by clinging
to the mast of his broken vessel.

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:19.570
He's rescued by the sailor Antonio, who ultimately
falls in love with him.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.720
While Ezra's character is off-stage for much
of the play's action, he does return to take

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.170
part in the comedy's amusing conclusion.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.989
Twelfth Night gave Ezra the chance to cut
his teeth performing live theatre for a TV

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:33.670
audience - an opportunity that any young actor
would certainly relish.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:37.510
So next time you see him chasing a receiver
as Spencer James, remember that the dude can

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.810
also do Shakespeare.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:41.110
"I'm just playing.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.410
Come on, dog."

